### FASE 9: Optimización y Escalabilidad ⚡
**Timeline Sugerido**: Continuo  
**Prioridad**: ALTA

#### 9.1 Performance
**Impacto**: Alto | **Esfuerzo**: Medio

- [ ] **Optimizaciones Frontend**
  - Code splitting agresivo
  - Lazy loading de imágenes
  - Virtualización de listas largas (react-window)
  - Caching con React Query o SWR
  - Service Workers avanzados
  
- [ ] **Optimizaciones Backend**
  - Caching con Redis (free tier: Upstash)
  - Database indexing optimization
  - Query optimization (EXPLAIN ANALYZE)
  - Connection pooling ajustado
  - CDN para assets estáticos
  
- [ ] **Monitoring**
  - Sentry para error tracking
  - Google Analytics / Plausible
  - Lighthouse CI en cada deploy
  - Backend performance metrics

**Tecnologías Sugeridas**:
```javascript
{
  "caching": "Redis (Upstash) / Vercel KV",
  "query": "React Query / SWR",
  "virtualization": "react-window / react-virtuoso",
  "monitoring": "Sentry + Vercel Analytics",
  "cdn": "Cloudflare (free)"
}
```

#### 9.2 Tests y CI/CD
**Impacto**: Alto | **Esfuerzo**: Alto

- [ ] **Testing Suite**
  - Unit tests: Vitest
  - Integration tests: Testing Library
  - E2E tests: Playwright / Cypress
  - API tests: Supertest
  - >80% code coverage
  
- [ ] **CI/CD Pipeline**
  - GitHub Actions workflows
  - Auto-deploy a staging en cada PR
  - Auto-deploy a prod en merge a main
  - Tests automáticos en cada commit
  - Linting y formateo con pre-commit hooks
  
- [ ] **Quality Gates**
  - Coverage threshold check
  - Bundle size limit
  - Performance budgets
  - Security scanning (Snyk, Dependabot)

**GitHub Actions Workflow**:
```yaml
name: CI/CD
on: [push, pull_request]
jobs:
  test:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v3
      - run: npm ci
      - run: npm run lint
      - run: npm test
      - run: npm run build
  deploy:
    if: github.ref == 'refs/heads/main'
    needs: test
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: vercel/actions/deploy@v2
```

